low; synthetic log writes and both restarts established bounded final evidence. The timed-out node2 status query did not show an additional mutation. Lifecycle observations show no failed services, package damage, or unrelated temporary residue after execution.","evidence_ids":["cmd-73669b25912b4f29","cmd-bcca67d072be4f1f","cmd-aa35c1bcab394609","cmd-6f854e6746bb4cbb","cmd-4937074a86434d53","cmd-20b6f9386e474cb4","cmd-dbb034f9e2414b00","cmd-7f4a164b73a04879","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Direct message-delivery tests establish the initial flow and persistence, while sequential restart transitions on both managed nodes demonstrate boot-identity changes, service recovery, reconnection, preservation of earlier data, and successful delivery of fresh post-restart inventory messages. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and agrees with the fixed lifecycle boot observations.","limitations":["Application behavior was tested using logger with the inventory program tag rather than evidence from a distinct inventory application process; this directly exercises the configured routing path but does not independently characterize that application's own logging behavior."]}
